From 9351218610606509bc80e979dbde86f64a1f8216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chai <tsaitomd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:17:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kernel-contract: the six fused prompt-chunk launches

The launches register with .usage = none: the 13.0 receipts are still owed,
the way glm_kv_paged_records.zig leaves its twins. The five-SM receipts from
kernel-contract-limits at nvcc 13.3.1 sit in measurements/pending_133.zig, so
the 13.3 lookup finds them and a release-compiler check compares the release
numbers instead of these. A test holds each launch against its window twin
(image, threads, shared bytes, opt-in, bound) and against every SM's limits.

bf16 sits at 123-124 (16-wide) and 211-251 (32-wide) registers, E4M3 at
128-204 and 248-255, all with no static shared bytes and a 256-thread bound.
The 32-wide E4M3 forms are at the ceiling on sm_80/sm_89.
---
 zig/src/core/contract/glm_fused_records.zig   | 55 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../contract/measurements/pending_133.zig     |  6 ++
 zig/src/core/contract/registry.zig            |  1 +
 zig/src/core/contract/registry_joins.zig      |  3 +-
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_kv8_test.zig        |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
